# TLSA (DANE) Record
# ====================
# TLSA records for DANE (DNS-based Authentication of Named Entities) enable
# TLS certificate verification via DNS, providing security beyond PKI.
#
# Format: <usage> <selector> <matching-type> <certificate-association-data>
#   - Usage: 0 = PKIX-TA, 1 = PKIX-EE, 2 = DANE-TA, 3 = DANE-EE
#   - Selector: 0 = Full Certificate, 1 = SPKI (Subject Public Key Info)
#   - Matching Type: 0 = Reserved, 1 = SHA-256, 2 = SHA-512
#   - Certificate Association Data: Hex-encoded hash
#
# For Trigger service (when deployed with HTTPS):
# Usage 3 (DANE-EE) - End Entity certificate only
# Selector 1 (SPKI) - Subject Public Key Info
# Matching Type 1 (SHA-256) - SHA-256 hash of SPKI
#
# NOTE: Authoritative TLSA records are defined in security/bind9/trigger.zone
# This file is provided for web servers that serve .well-known/ for compatibility.
#
# For more information: RFC 6698 (DANE)
# https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6698
#
# Placeholder - generate actual hashes when certificates are deployed:
# Example for port 443:
#_443._tcp  3 1 1 <SHA-256 hash of SPKI in hex>
#
# Example for port 8080:
#_8080._tcp  3 1 1 <SHA-256 hash of SPKI in hex>
